# C-Programs

This repository contains basic C programming experiments completed as part of my first-year B.Tech (AIML) programming laboratory.

## Experiments Included

### 1. Hello World Program
- Print "Hello, World!" using C.

### 2. Print Different Data Types
- Print values of:
  - Integer (int)
  - Float (float)
  - Character (char)

### 3. Input Using scanf()
- Read integer, float, and character values from the user using `scanf()` and display them.

### 4. Print Array
- Create and print arrays of different data types.

### 5. Array Using scanf()
- Accept array elements from the user using `scanf()` and display them.

## Technologies Used
- Language: C
- Compiler: GCC / Turbo C / Code::Blocks / VS Code

## Purpose
This repository is created to practice basic C programming concepts and improve programming skills.

